      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened on May 21, 1888, called Poe; Isaac Piper was its first postmaster before the town was renamed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/wells_kansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1910, Wells had 42 residents and operated a money‑order post office, express office, and a single rural route.",
